{
 "about": "A third kind of game built with the same tools, after the structure of the official farming sample: take the rake from the rack (F), walk to a plot and use it (E) to till; fetch seeds from the basket (F), use them on the tilled plot (E); the crop grows in two steps on the plot's own timer; harvest the ripe pumpkin (F) and sell it at the stall (F) for a point. What is new here next to the other two games: a signal that carries a string (the tool in hand) from the character to whichever plot the character stands on; state on each plot (its stage, whether somebody stands on it) so that two plots do not get in each other's way; the crop's looks are prefabs owned by the plot and swapped; fruit is a currency in the character's backpack; the skill is handed out when the first tool is taken. Climbing is off and a wall stands at each end, so that the script can walk into a wall to be at a known place. Played through as designed on its first run in the game, 2026-10-11. Prints: FM_READY, FM_GO, FM_TOOL 1, FM_TILL, FM_TOOL 2, FM_PLANT, FM_SPROUT, FM_RIPE, FM_HARVEST, FM_FRUIT n, FM_SOLD, FM_SCORE n, FM_VICTORY (or FM_TIME_UP), FM_AT x every two seconds.",
